The rest of Sigil is licensed under the GNU AGPL-3.0; the files in this directory keep
their Apache-2.0 license.

Vendored files: model.rs, npz.rs, phonemize.rs, preprocess.rs and tokenize.rs (from src/),
plus mod.rs (from src/lib.rs). Not vendored: src/download.rs (hf-hub downloader), src/ffi.rs
(iOS/Android C FFI), build.rs, examples, tests and scripts.

Changes made for Sigil (2026-09-28, P1-S0a):
- Every file carries an SPDX / attribution header.
- The `espeak` Cargo feature is always on: its #[cfg] gates and the non-espeak fallbacks in
  phonemize.rs and model.rs were removed; tests gated on the feature run unconditionally.
- Module paths: `crate::…` became `super::…`; lib.rs became mod.rs, without the `download` and
  `ffi` modules, with `#![allow(dead_code)]` for the unused library surface and an allow-list of
  the six clippy style lints the upstream code triggers (the code itself is unchanged).
- model.rs: the ONNX session is built through Sigil's shared ONNX Runtime factory
  (`neural_audio::ort_session::build_session`, explicit CPU execution provider, spinning off)
  instead of `ort::Session::builder()`; `write_wav` logs through `tracing` instead of `println!`.
- hub.rs is new: it replaces download.rs. It keeps upstream's `ModelConfig` schema, requires plain
  file names in a Hub repo's config.json, reuses an existing hf-hub cache snapshot, and otherwise
  downloads one file at a time with Sigil's HTTP client into the app-data folder.
- The `ort` dependency follows Sigil's own version instead of kittentts' `=2.0.0-rc.11` pin, and
  `hf-hub` is no longer a dependency.
